| actual source | actual destination | old source rank | actual contribution | destination before | destination after |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 0 | 1 | 0.5 | 0.425 | 0.2875 | 0.7124999999999999 |
\image(figures/page_rank_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual uniform base, dangling mass and edge addition for the first two-page update.)
\alttext(A one-update budget returns the observed vector with converged=false; the destination receives both the uniform base and the actual directed edge contribution.)

> Retain the original three-page graph

The original graph has0→2,1→2 and2→2. There are no dangling pages. Each of
pages0 and1 receives only uniform teleportation, so its stationary score
is(1−d)/3=.05 for d=.85; the remaining.9 belongs to page2. The self-loop retains
page2’s link-following mass. These values follow from the graph model and are
independently checked against the actual canonical result below.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/page_rank_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/page_rank.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <numeric>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::page_rank_trace(3,
                                        dm::algorithms::page_rank_demo_edges());
    std::print("Actual complete updates: {}. Actual edge additions: {}. Actual strict-change convergence: " "{}. Actual score sum: {:.15f}.\n\n",
               t.run.iterations, t.run.edge_transfers, t.run.converged,
               std::accumulate(t.run.scores.begin(), t.run.scores.end(), 0.));
    std::print("| page | actual returned rank |\n| ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.run.scores.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {:.15f} |\n", i, t.run.scores[i]);
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(t.run.scores, {"page0", "page1", "page2"},
                                     "actual rank");
    p.title("Original three-page graph: actual stationary ranks").x_label(
        "original page ID").y_label("actual returned rank").y_limits(0, 1.1).save_svg("build/page_rank_original.svg");
}
```
