> Follow actual convergence on the dangling graph

For0→1 with page1 dangling, let r_0 be page0’s stationary score. The update
equation gives r_0=(1−d)/2+dr_1/2 with r_1=1−r_0, hence r_0=1/(2+d). The table
compares native returned scores with that analytical value for several damping
factors. Every plotted state change comes from an actual complete update; no
report-side power iteration is used.

This example’s nonconstant mode contracts by−d/2, so the general worst-case
factor d is conservative here. Higher damping can require more updates, but a
universal wall-clock statement cannot be read from this one graph or from
iteration counts alone.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/page_rank_convergence.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/page_rank.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    std::vector<dm::graphics::RGBA> colors{{37, 99, 235, 255},
                                           {220, 38, 38, 255},
                                           {22, 163, 74, 255}};
    std::vector<std::string> labels;
    std::print("| damping | actual updates | actual page0 | analytic page0 | actual final change | " "exact-model bound diagnostic | converged |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- " "|\n");
    std::size_t color = 0;
    for (double d : {.5, .85, .99}) {
        auto t =
            dm::algorithms::page_rank_trace(2, {{0, 1}},
                                            {d, 1e-12, 1000, 100000});
        std::vector<double> x, y;
        for (auto &s : t.iterations) {
            x.push_back(s.ordinal);
            y.push_back(std::log10(std::max(s.l1_change, 1e-18)));
        }
        auto label = std::format("d={}", d);
        labels.push_back(label);
        p.lines(x, y, label, colors[color]).points(x, y, colors[color++], 3.);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {:.15f} | {:.15f} | {:.5e} | {:.5e} | {} |\n",
                   d, t.run.iterations, t.run.scores[0], 1 / (2 + d),
                   t.run.last_change, t.run.contraction_bound, t.run.converged);
    }
    p.title("Dangling two-page graph: actual L1 state changes").x_label(
        "actual completed power updates").y_label("log10(max(actual L1 change,1e-18))").save_svg("build/page_rank_convergence.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| damping | actual updates | actual page0 | analytic page0 | actual final change | exact-model bound diagnostic | converged |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| 0.5 | 20 | 0.400000000000091 | 0.400000000000000 | 9.09495e-13 | 9.09495e-13 | true |
| 0.85 | 33 | 0.350877192982375 | 0.350877192982456 | 5.45564e-13 | 3.09153e-12 | true |
| 0.99 | 40 | 0.334448160535218 | 0.334448160535117 | 6.08458e-13 | 6.02373e-11 | true |
\image(figures/page_rank_convergence.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual state-change histories and analytical two-page stationary checks for three damping factors.)
\alttext(The bound column is the exact-model contraction diagnostic; it excludes arithmetic error and is not advertised as a floating-point certificate.)

> Multiplicity, empty graphs and finite budgets

Duplicate links split a source’s mass by its full occurrence count; changing
their multiplicity can change the stochastic model. No-edge graphs are entirely
dangling and preserve the uniform vector. At d=0 the next vector is uniform
regardless of edges. The control chart displays log10(update count+1), while the
table retains raw update counts. A nonempty zero-update run returns its uniform
initialization with converged=false; an empty graph returns an empty vector with
converged=true, provided no invalid edge or numerical control is supplied.

Complete edge endpoints, finite d in[0,1) and finite positive tolerance are
validated before graph allocation and iteration. One update costs O(n+E), and
ordinary storage is O(n+E). Every source uses the unchanged old rank vector;
actual additions are grouped by ascending source and original occurrence order
within that source, preserving the original valid-input numerical trajectory.

The owned trace includes graph endpoints, initial/final scores and every
complete update/edge addition. Logical admission counts4+2E+2n + I(1+2n)+T, for
I actual updates and T actual edge transfers. The four root units represent
vertex count and three numerical controls; fixed diagnostic fields are included
within their records. Default1000000, zero disables. Base admission precedes
graph/input copies, and online admission precedes each owned iteration/transfer.
This is not a byte or peak-memory bound, and failure returns no partial trace.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/page_rank_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/page_rank.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <numeric>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<std::string> labels{"zero budget", "one update", "all dangling",
                                    "zero damping", "duplicate links", "empty"};
    std::vector<dm::algorithms::PageRankRun> runs;
    runs.push_back(dm::algorithms::page_rank_run(2, {{0, 1}}, {.85, 1e-12, 0, 0}));
    runs.push_back(dm::algorithms::page_rank_run(2, {{0, 1}}, {.85, 1e-12, 1, 0}));
    runs.push_back(dm::algorithms::page_rank_run(2, {}));
    runs.push_back(dm::algorithms::page_rank_run(3,
                                                 dm::algorithms::page_rank_demo_edges(),
                                                 {0., 1e-12, 1000, 0}));
    runs.push_back(dm::algorithms::page_rank_run(3,
                                                 {{0, 1}, {0, 1}, {0, 2},
                                                  {1, 0}, {2, 0}}));
    runs.push_back(dm::algorithms::page_rank_run(0, {}));
    std::vector<double> updates;
    std::print("| control | actual complete updates | actual score sum | actual last change | converged " "|\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < runs.size(); ++i) {
        auto &r = runs[i];
        updates.push_back(std::log10(1. + double(r.iterations)));
        std::print("| {} | {} | {:.12f} | {:.5e} | {} |\n", labels[i],
                   r.iterations,
                   std::accumulate(r.scores.begin(), r.scores.end(), 0.),
                   r.last_change, r.converged);
    }
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(updates, labels, "actual update counts");
    p.title("PageRank controls: finite budgets and graph models").x_label(
        "explicit native graph/control").y_label("log10(actual power updates +1)").save_svg("build/page_rank_controls.svg");
}
```
